<title>USA: TVA Watts Bar nuke reduced for testing.</title>
<headline>TVA Watts Bar nuke reduced for testing.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear's Watts Bar unit was reduced to 97 percent of its 1,170 megawatt capacity early Tuesday for testing, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Spring City, Tenn., is undergoing testing for line blockage. Following x-raying, plant operators will &quot;then decide whether to increase power or shut down,&quot; the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>As a matter of policy, TVA declines to comment on the status of its nuclear power plants.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
